{%- comment -%}
  A content page — anything the studio writes that doesn't warrant its own
  template. Port of app/about/page.tsx and the PageHeading primitive in
  components/ui/section.tsx.

  ABOUT US NO LONGER USES THIS. Brief §13 asked for the About page to be
  "visual", which this plain title-plus-rich-text shape cannot give it, so it
  got its own `page.about` template and `sections/about-story.liquid`
  instead (built 2026-09-22) — see that section's own comment. This one
  stays as the fallback for a page nobody has built a dedicated template for
  yet (currently none are assigned it; My Account and 404 use their own
  templates too).

  The heading and the body come from the Shopify page itself. Where the page
  has no content yet the labelled placeholder renders at final size.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg">
  <div class="wl-measure">
    <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: page.title, label: 'page heading' %}
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-6 text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {%- if page.content != blank -%}
        {{ page.content }}
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'copy', value: '', label: 'intro', lines: 2 %}
        <div class="mt-8">{% render 'copy', value: '', label: 'body', lines: 5 %}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Page",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The heading and body are the Shopify page's own title and content. Edit them under Content → Pages, not here. An empty page renders a labelled placeholder at final size rather than a blank screen." }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
